 # 8\. Functional Requirements

 ## FR-01 — User Registration

 The system should allow users to create an account.

 ## FR-02 — User Authentication

 Users should be able to sign in and sign out.

 ## FR-03 — Project Creation

 Users should be able to create a new comic project.

 ## FR-04 — Story Input

 Users should provide:

 - Story idea
- Genre
- Style
- Tone
- Number of pages
- Panels per page

 ## FR-05 — AI Story Generation

 The system should send the user's requirements to Gemini and generate structured comic content.

 ## FR-06 — Character Generation

 The system should generate character profiles.

 ## FR-07 — Page Generation

 The system should divide the story into pages.

 ## FR-08 — Panel Generation

 Each page should contain individual panels.

 ## FR-09 — Dialogue Generation

 Panels should support character dialogue and captions.

 ## FR-10 — Content Editing

 Users should be able to modify AI-generated content.

 ## FR-11 — Panel Regeneration

 Users should be able to regenerate an individual panel.

 ## FR-12 — Dialogue Rewriting

 Users should be able to request alternative dialogue.

 ## FR-13 — Story Continuation

 Users should be able to continue an existing comic.

 ## FR-14 — Project Saving

 Projects should be saved to persistent storage.

 ## FR-15 — Comic Preview

 Users should be able to read the comic in a dedicated reader.

 ## FR-16 — Export

 Users should be able to export the comic.

---

 # 9\. Non-Functional Requirements

 ### Performance

 The application should provide responsive interactions and meaningful loading feedback during AI generation.

 ### Security

 - API keys must remain server-side.
- User projects must be isolated.
- API requests must be validated.
- AI output must be validated before database storage.

 ### Usability

 The interface should be understandable to users without technical knowledge.

 ### Scalability

 The architecture should allow future additions such as:

 - Image generation
- Collaboration
- Public comic sharing
- Mobile applications

 ### Maintainability

 AI operations, database logic and UI components should remain modular.

